# Aegis fix catalog #092 — Service image pull denied / not found
#
# Tier:       4 · Advanced
# Category:   image_pull_failure (auto-diagnosed from the log below)
# Engine:     deterministic rule engine — no AI involved
#
# CI log:
#   | Error response from daemon: pull access denied for acme/api, repository does not exist or may require 'docker login'
#   | manifest unknown docker
#
# How it is solved:
#   CREATE .dockerignore
#     - Created .dockerignore — without it, docker build sends node_modules, .git, and test files to the build context
#     - this increases build time, image size, and can leak secrets from .env files into the image
#     - Added secret file patterns to .dockerignore (*.pem, *.key, *.p12, *.pfx, ...) — if these files exist in the build context, COPY . . would include them in the image layer, permanently exposing secrets in docker history
#
# Apply:      git apply 04-advanced/092-image_pull_failure.diff
diff --git a/.dockerignore b/.dockerignore
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.dockerignore
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+.git
+.github
+.gitignore
+node_modules
+.npm
+npm-debug.log*
+.eslintcache
+dist
+build
+out
+coverage
+.env
+.env.*
+!.env.example
+*.md
+docs/
+test/
+tests/
+.DS_Store
+Thumbs.db
+docker-compose*.yml
+.dockerignore
+Dockerfile*
+# Secrets — must never reach the Docker build context
+*.pem
+*.key
+*.p12
+*.pfx
+.env.production
+.env.local
+secrets/
+credentials/
+*.secret
+id_rsa
+id_ed25519
+*.crt
+kubeconfig
